1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,648
My heart beats twice as fast because I sold half my life to save a drowning stranger.

2
00:00:06,948 --> 00:00:14,556
The broker said I had thousands of hours to spare. He paid me cash for every single missing thump.

3
00:00:14,856 --> 00:00:22,056
At first, I felt invincible. I bought the car, the apartment, all the things I never thought I could afford.

4
00:00:22,356 --> 00:00:30,660
Then the fatigue crept in. My chest felt hollow, like an empty drum echoing in a vast, cold room.

5
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:37,176
I called the broker to buy my time back, to reverse the trade before my engine completely ran out.

6
00:00:37,476 --> 00:00:45,444
The line was dead. The neon shop downtown was completely gone, replaced by a brick wall covered in dust.

7
00:00:45,744 --> 00:00:54,024
A passerby walked right through me, dropping his coffee as a sudden, freezing chill filled the empty street.

8
00:00:54,324 --> 00:01:01,092
I looked down at my hands and saw they were translucent, glowing faintly like fading embers in the dark.

9
00:01:01,392 --> 00:01:07,584
I didn't sell half my life. I sold all of it three days ago in that alleyway accident.

10
00:01:07,884 --> 00:01:13,236
If I am already dead and gone... who is currently beating inside your chest right now?
